rea. Flooding is ongoing. Trees and debris larger\nthan telephone poles have been observed flowing down the\nriver. Between 1.0 and 2.5 inches of rain have fallen.\nAdditional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are possible\nwith higher amounts possible in the upper Yentna Basin.\n- For Yentna River at Lake Creek:\nAt 7:51am the stage was 20.7 feet.\nFlood Stage is 20.5 feet.\nForecast: A crest slightly above 22 feet late tonight and\ninto early Wednesday morning.\n\nImpacts:\nBetween 21 and 22 feet, several lodges may have water in or\naround low-lying cabins.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Stay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further information.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSAFC"],"WMOidentifier":["WGAK88 PAFC 042354"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 1 PM AKDT FRIDAY"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.PAFC.FA.W.0005.000000T0000Z-260807T2100Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-07T13:00:00-08:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLS"],"NationalWeatherService":["FAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.15496853d81a7696b9600e483af722795486a1d2.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-150.76,62.57],[-150.48,62.55],[-150.48,62.38],[-150.52,62.32],[-150.56,62.28],[-150.62,62.21],[-150.7,62.18],[-150.77,62.22],[-150.83,62.31],[-150.98,62.38],[-151.08,62.45],[-151.05,62.53],[-150.76,62.57]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.15496853d81a7696b9600e483af722795486a1d2.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.15496853d81a7696b9600e483af722795486a1d2.001.1","areaDesc":"Central Susitna Valley","geocode":{"SAME":["002170"],"UGC":["AKZ747"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/AKZ747"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-08-04T08:45:00-08:00","effective":"2026-08-04T08:45:00-08:00","onset":"2026-08-04T08:45:00-08:00","expires":"2026-08-05T17:00:00-08:00","ends":"2026-08-05T17:00:00-08:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Expected","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Anchorage AK","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 4 at 8:45AM AKDT until August 5 at 5:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Petersville Area\n\n* WHEN...Until 500 PM AKDT Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Low-water\ncrossings are inundated with water and may not be passable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 842 AM AKDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain across the warned area. Flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly. Between 2 and 3 inches\nof rain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to\n1.5 inches are possible.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Stay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further information.\n\nTurn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nIn hilly terrain there are hundreds of low water crossings which are\npotentially dangerous in heavy rain. Do not attempt to cross flooded\nroads. Find an alternate route.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLWAFC"],"WMOidentifier":["WGAK48 PAFC 041645"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING IN EFFECT UNTIL 5 PM AKDT WEDNESDAY"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.PAFC.FA.W.0006.260804T1645Z-260806T0100Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-05T17:00:00-08:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLW"],"NationalWeatherService":["FAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.368f4c6289324c0eb7a474337c729fc029de21cc.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[144.55,14.13],[144.57,14.17],[144.79,14.06],[144.67,13.87],[144.47,14.01],[144.55,14.13]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.368f4c6289324c0eb7a474337c729fc029de21cc.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.368f4c6289324c0eb7a474337c729fc029de21cc.001.1","areaDesc":"Guam Coastal Waters; Rota Coastal Waters","geocode":{"SAME":["065151","065152"],"UGC":["PMZ151","PMZ152"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/PMZ151","https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/PMZ152"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-08-05T21:17:00+10:00","effective":"2026-08-05T21:17:00+10:00","onset":"2026-08-05T21:17:00+10:00","expires":"2026-08-05T21:45:00+10:00","ends":"2026-08-05T21:45:00+10:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Special Marine Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Tiyan GU","headline":"Special Marine Warning issued August 5 at 9:17PM ChST until August 5 at 9:45PM ChST by NWS Tiyan GU","description":"SMWGUM\n\nTHE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE IN TIYAN HAS ISSUED A\n\n* SPECIAL MARINE WARNING FOR...\nGUAM COASTAL WATERS...\nROTA COASTAL WATERS...\n\n* UNTIL 945 PM CHST.\n\n* AT 917 PM CHST, A SEVERE THUNDERSTORM PRODUCING WATERSPOUTS WAS\nLOCATED 27 NM NORTHWEST OF RITIDIAN BUOY, MOVING SOUTHEAST AT 15\nKNOTS.\n\nHAZARD...WATERSPOUTS AND WIND GUSTS TO 40 KNOTS.\n\nSOURCE...RADAR INDICATED.\n\nIMPACT...WATERSPOUTS CAN EASILY OVERTURN BOATS AND CREATE LOCALLY\nHAZARDOUS SEAS. SMALL CRAFT COULD BE DAMAGED IN BRIEFLY\nHIGHER WINDS AND SUDDENLY HIGHER WAVES.\n\n* LOCATIONS IMPACTED INCLUDE...\nMAINLY NORTHERN GUAM WATERS AND WESTERN ROTA WATERS.","instruction":"MOVE TO SAFE HARBOR UNTIL HAZARDOUS WEATHER PASSES.\n\nBOATERS SHOULD SEEK SAFE HARBOR IMMEDIATELY UNTIL THIS STORM PASSES.\nWIND GUSTS 34 KNOTS OR GREATER, HIGH WAVES, DANGEROUS LIGHTNING, AND\nHEAVY RAIN ARE POSSIBLE WITH THIS STORM.\n\nTHUNDERSTORMS CAN PRODUCE SUDDEN WATERSPOUTS. WATERSPOUTS CAN EASILY\nOVERTURN BOATS AND CREATE LOCALLY HAZARDOUS SEAS. SEEK SAFE HARBOR\nIMMEDIATELY.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["SMWGUM"],"WMOidentifier":["WHMY50 PGUM 051117"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-08-05T11:15:00-00:00...storm...302DEG...14KT...14.07,144.56"],"maxWindGust":["34 knots"],"maxHailSize":["0.00"],"waterspoutDetection":["OBSERVED"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.PGUM.MA.W.0016.260805T1117Z-260805T1145Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-05T21:45:00+10:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["SMW"],"NationalWeatherService":["MAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3a93f3780ac3d991c1eb7b7fff2e643cca69a1df.002.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-93.37,40.29],[-93.77,40.4],[-93.77,40.57],[-93.38,40.58],[-93.37,40.29]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3a93f3780ac3d991c1eb7b7fff2e643cca69a1df.002.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3a93f3780ac3d991c1eb7b7fff2e643cca69a1df.002.1","areaDesc":"Mercer, MO","geocode":{"SAME":["029129"],"UGC":["MOC129"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/MOC129"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.039863342af3389063e3662241d2eaea2898fc29.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.039863342af3389063e3662241d2eaea2898fc29.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-05T05:54:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-05T06:16:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-05T06:16:00-05:00","onset":"20